{
  "name": "viewmodel_editor",
  "description": "Creates and manages view models and their instances. Supports commands like,listViewModels: Lists all view models; createViewModels: Creates view models with properties; createViewModelInstances: Creates instances of a view model; addProperties: Adds properties to existing view models. A viewModel-typed property references another view model by viewModelId (preferred) or viewModelName, which may name one created in the same call; databind: Makes the value of an object's property come from a viewmodel instance. When binding strings to text, you must bind to the Text Run, not the Text object itself. Re-running databind on an already-bound object property retargets the existing bind. Properties on nested viewmodels need path when several routes reach them; isRelative makes the bind resolve by names from the bound instance (the relative toggle); modifyDataBind: Modifies an existing data bind's direction (toTarget, toSource, twoWay), once flag, source-to-target ordering, attached converter, source path, or relative flag; bindViewModelToArtboard: Binds a viewmodel instance to an artboard; bindViewModelToComponent: Sets a component placement's own data context (the Model/Path rows in the inspector). Use this - not raw property writes - to point each placement of the same component at its own viewmodel property, clear it back to inherit, or assign a specific instance. Accepts multiple placements at once. Not available for stateful components (their instance is auto-managed); listViewModelInstances: Lists all view model instances from a view model; listDataBinds: Lists existing data binds with their source paths and flags; createConverters: Creates data converters to transform a bound value (for example convertToString so a number property can drive a text run). Pass the returned id as a binding's converterId in databind, then tune settings with query_core_object_tool setPropertyValues. Use a group to chain several transforms into one converter (its children are created or reused in the same call) and a formula for arithmetic. Check listConverters first and reuse a match: converters cannot be deleted here, so one created by mistake stays in the data panel for the user to remove; listConverters: Lists existing converters with their type and id, so one can be reused instead of creating a duplicate; listDataEnums: Lists enums (the Enums section of the data panel) with their values; createDataEnums: Creates enums and their values. Create the enum before an enum property that uses it; addDataEnumValues: Appends values to an existing enum; removeDataEnumValues: Removes values from an enum; deleteDataEnums: Deletes whole enums and their values. Needs force: true to delete one that still backs properties, and sweeps any library assets the removal leaves unused. An enum property is a viewModelProperties entry with propertyType enum plus enumName or enumId; ",
  "inputSchema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "command": {
        "type": "string",
        "enum": [
          "listViewModels",
          "createViewModels",
          "createViewModelInstances",
          "addProperties",
          "databind",
          "modifyDataBind",
          "bindViewModelToArtboard",
          "bindViewModelToComponent",
          "listViewModelInstances",
          "listDataBinds",
          "createConverters",
          "listConverters",
          "listDataEnums",
          "createDataEnums",
          "addDataEnumValues",
          "removeDataEnumValues",
          "deleteDataEnums"
        ]
      },
      "data": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "listViewModels": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {}
          },
          "createViewModels": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "viewModels": {
                "type": "array",
                "items": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "name": {
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    "viewModelProperties": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "oneOf": [
                          {
                            "type": "object",
                            "properties": {
                              "name": {
                                "type": "string"
                              },
                              "propertyType": {
                                "enum": [
                                  "string",
                                  "boolean",
                                  "color",
                                  "number",
                                  "trigger",
                                  "artboard",
                                  "image",
                                  "font",
                                  "blob"
                                ]
                              }
                            }
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "object",
